# /v2.html was an unfinished redesign draft that sat on the production domain
# for three days. It was removed from site/ (preserved at launch/v2-draft.html,
# which is gitignored) and it is absent from both the working tree and git —
# and Netlify kept serving it anyway across four deploys. Rather than keep
# hunting for where the deploy bundle picks it up, this makes it unreachable
# whether or not the file is present.
#
# The trailing ! is load-bearing. Without it Netlify serves a matching static
# file in preference to a redirect rule, which is exactly the case here.

/v2.html    /    301!
